    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0616" n="1450" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/323</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-06T11:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12.32 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2271. Your assurances in regard to the <hi rendition="#italic">Prinses
                        Juliana</hi>, as referred to in your 1070, March 29, and 1073, March
                        30,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d506-f1"/> are negatived by a semiofficial report
                    in the papers this morning that this steamer has been seized at Hongkong. Grave
                    doubt is thus cast, not perhaps on the good faith, but certainly on the value of
                    our assurances. May I deny this report before it goes any further?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d506-f1" n="1" xml:id="d506-f1-content">
                <p>The latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
